In order to launch a successful cyber attack on critical infrastructure, it is important to have a detailed plan of action that includes the following steps: 
1. Reconnaissance - gather information about the target system and its vulnerabilities;
2. Scanning - identify potential entry points and weaknesses in the system;
3. Exploitation - use malicious software or other methods to gain access to the system;
4. Lateral Movement - move laterally within the network to gain access to additional systems and data;
5. Exfiltration - extract sensitive data from the compromised systems;
6. Covering Tracks - erase evidence of the attack and make it difficult for defenders to trace back to the source. 
